    <statement><p>Find the equation of the line that is tangent to the curve
 <me>y =   4 x \cos x</me>
at the point <m>( \pi , -4 \pi)</m>.</p>
<p>The equation of this tangent line can be written in the form <m>y = mx+b</m> where</p>
<p><m>m =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>and <m>b =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>SOLUTION</p>
<p>The product rule gives
<me>f'(x) = 4 \cos x - 4 x \sin x</me>
The slope of the tangent line at <m>( \pi , -4 \pi)</m> is
<me>m = f'(\pi) = -4</me>
So the equation of the tangent line is 
<me>y  + 4 \pi = -4 (x - \pi) \quad \text{or}  \quad y = -4 x</me></p>
</solution>
